   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "To measure a larger current without burning the delicate coil, we place a low resistance in parallel.",
    "imageQuery": "galvanometer movement coil vintage",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "working"
    },
    "visualWas": {
     "kind": "sketch",
     "sketch": "kirchhoff",
     "caption": "",
     "params": {
      "labelA": "Itotal = 10 A"
     },
     "items": []
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "First, we calculate the multiplying power m, which is the total current divided by the meter current.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "m = I / Iₘ",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "The total current is 10 amperes, while the meter full scale deflection current is 10 milliamperes.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "compare",
     "caption": "",
     "items": [
      {
       "label": "Total I = 10 A",
       "symbol": "⚡"
      },
      {
       "label": "Meter Im = 10 mA",
       "symbol": "🎛️"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Converting 10 amperes to milliamperes gives 10000 milliamperes, yielding a multiplying factor of exactly 1000.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "m = 10 A / 0.01 A = 1000",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "The standard shunt formula states that shunt resistance equals meter resistance divided by m minus one.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Rₛₕ = Rₘ / (m - 1)",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Substitute the known values: coil resistance is 99 ohms and the multiplier minus one equals 999.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Rₛₕ = 99 / (1000 - 1)",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Dividing 99 ohms by 999 yields 0.099099 ohms, which rounds neatly to 0.099 ohms.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Rₛₕ = 99 / 999 ≈ 0.099 Ω",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Candidates frequently make the mistake of dividing by m directly, incorrectly arriving at 0.100 ohms.",
    "imageQuery": "",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "sketch",
     "sketch": "misconception",
     "caption": "",
     "params": {
      "labelA": "Rm / m = 0.100 Ω",
      "labelB": "Rm / (m-1) = 0.099 Ω"
     },
     "items": []
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "This low-resistance shunt bypasses almost all current, allowing the meter to read high currents safely.",
    "imageQuery": "printed circuit board copper tracks",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "bars",
